  "id": "perceived-susceptibility",
  "term": "perceived susceptibility",
  "definition": "Perceived susceptibility is a person’s belief about how likely they are to be affected by a threat, such as becoming infected by a virus. In protection motivation theory, greater perceived susceptibility can be linked with stronger use of protective behaviors.",
